# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0017933> (hypertrophic cardiomyopathy and renal tubular disease due to mitochondrial DNA mutation)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "Orphanet:324525") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0017933> "Hypertrophic cardiomyopathy and renal tubular disease due to mitochondrial DNA mutation is a mitochondrial oxidative phosphorylation disorder characterized by hypertrophic and dilated cardiomyopathy, failure to thrive, myopathy with generalized hypotonia and increased creatine kinase, developmental delay and/or regression with cerebral atrophy on brain MRI, renal manifestations including chronic renal failure, renal tubular acidosis and lactic acidosis. Additional clinical features include seizures and respiratory failure.")
